{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
At the [G]east end of town at the [Em]foot of the hill,
there‘s a [D]chimney so tall it says [C]Aragon [G]Mill.
But there‘s [G]no smoke at all comin’ [Em]out of it’s stack,
since the [D]mill has shut down it‘s [C]never coming [G]back.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Refrain}
And the [G]only tune I hear is the [Em]sound of the wind,
as she [D]blows through the town weave and [C]spin, [D]weave and [G]spin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
There's no [G]children playin‘ in the [Em]dark narrow streets,
since the [D]mill has shut down, it's so [C]quiet that I can't [G]sleep.
The [G]mill has shut down, but it's the [Em]only life I know,
tell me, [D]what will I do, tell me, [C]where will I [G]go?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Refrain}
[G]And the only tune I hear is the [Em]sound of the wind,
as she [D]blows through the town weave and [C]spin, [D]weave and [G]spin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I'm too [G]old to work, and I'm too [Em]young to die.
Tell me, [D]where will I go now, my [C]family and [G]I?
There‘s no [G]use anymore for these [Em]cotton mills it seems,
but the [D]sound of the loom [C]still haunts my [G]dreams.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Weave and [D]spin...
[D]Weave and [G]spin...
(6x fade out)
{end_of_verse}
